# The verify gate's performance list for the cbp2025 host: 4 traces, one per
# workload family, all of them small.
#
# Sizing this is a real trade and the trade is stated here rather than
# hidden. G5 asks one question: does the mechanism move the metric the way
# the paper says. It is a direction check, not a score. The score comes from
# screening-60.list and training-105.list in stage 4, which keep all six
# families and every trace in them.
#
# What the length costs. The gate runs the whole list twice per integration
# attempt, feature-on and feature-off, and the loop allows six attempts. This
# cluster offers 4 cbp2025 slots, so a 4-trace list is exactly one wave per
# feature state. Measured on the first full gate run, the 8-trace list it
# replaces took about 16 minutes of simulator per attempt, or an hour and a
# half across six attempts, and that is time the agent does not get to spend
# fixing the port.
#
# What the length buys, and does not. Four traces is enough to tell "the
# mechanism reaches the metric" from "it does not". It is not enough to
# report a gain from, and nothing downstream treats it as one: the gate's
# warn_threshold is explicitly non-blocking for the same reason, because the
# port is untuned when it runs.
#
# The traces are the smallest member of four of the six families. media and
# compress are absent: their smallest members are 94 MiB and 109 MiB, which
# is two to three times everything here.
int/int_13_trace.gz
web/web_21_trace.gz
fp/fp_1_trace.gz
infra/infra_8_trace.gz
